    studyNotes:["Numbers is not simply a list of censuses: narrative and law repeatedly interpret one another.","The spy narrative in chapters 13–14 is the major turning point, transforming the wilderness from a journey into a generation-long judgment.","Balaam's story introduces an outsider who recognizes Israel's blessed status while Israel itself repeatedly fails.","The final chapters deliberately shift from wilderness failure toward inheritance and preparation."],
